# A sample /STARTUP.BAT -- copy it to / and edit. It runs at power-on.
# If one you wrote wedges the machine, turn it off in F7 > Run STARTUP.BAT,
# or start the emulator with --no-startup.bat. Your own copy is never
# overwritten.
# Aliases live in RAM, so they are defined here every boot.

# the CP/M programs, each through a .SUB on A: that ends in EXIT,
# so quitting the program comes all the way back to this shell
ALIAS MBASIC CPM K-MBAS
ALIAS TURBO  CPM K-TURBO
ALIAS WS     CPM K-WS

# odds and ends
ALIAS LL DIR A
